Parabellum License

Copyright © 2026 Juan Jose Rojas Garcia and contributors to Parabellum. All rights reserved.

1. WHAT IS ALLOWED

The following is allowed:
- viewing and reading the source code in this repository;
- forking this repository on GitHub only to prepare changes and propose them by pull request to this repository;
- using Parabellum as distributed in its official downloads: the releases of this repository and the project's Google Drive catalog;
- sharing the official Parabellum zip unmodified and free of charge (for example, giving it to someone on a USB drive), as it comes, with the license and third-party notices it contains.

2. WHAT IS NOT ALLOWED WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM JUAN

Without written permission from Juan Jose Rojas Garcia, the following is not allowed:
- redistributing the code or the executables of Parabellum, modified or not, except sharing the official zip as allowed in point 1;
- publishing your own or derivative versions of Parabellum;
- setting up your own services or infrastructure based on the code (bridges, catalogs, Parabellum servers);
- commercial use.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS

Whoever submits a pull request:
- grants Juan Jose Rojas Garcia a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free and irrevocable license to use, modify and distribute their contribution as part of Parabellum;
- declares that they have the right to grant it.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Third-party components keep their own licenses. They are listed in AVISOS-DE-TERCEROS.md.

5. NO WARRANTY

Parabellum is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. The author is not liable for any damages arising from its use.
